module moed-criminal-local-rules.local-rules

import core.frcrimp45.{ frcrimp45 }

// The Eastern District of Missouri's own periods in a criminal case.
// FRCrimP 45(a) computes a period "in any local rule" of a criminal case,
// so these count under frcrimp45. For good cause the court may extend or
// shorten any time limit the rules impose (L.R. 1.05). The disclosure and
// pretrial motion deadlines are set by an order entered at or after
// arraignment (L.R. 3.05), not by rule. Stated in the rules but not
// declared: the redacted sealing material within three business days of a
// motion for sealing (L.R. 13.05(A)(4)(c)), counted in business days,
// which frcrimp45 does not count; the six months a granted warrant
// sealing lasts before a motion to continue it (L.R. 13.05(C)(4)(c)) and
// the Clerk's five years for pen register and similar originals (L.R.
// 13.05(C)(2)), stated in months and years; the further 14 days a denial
// of sealing stays after an appellate ruling affirms it (L.R.
// 13.05(A)(4)(g)), which runs from a ruling of another court; the
// summary judgment, fee and costs oppositions (L.R. 4.01(E), (F)) and the
// civil unsealing periods (L.R. 13.05(B)), civil rules; and the
// convicted defendant's counsel's notice of appeal or of the defendant's
// decision not to appeal "within the time permitted for an appeal" (L.R.
// 12.07(A)), which is FRAP 4(b)'s period, lit/frcrimp's. The earlier
// E.D. Mo. criminal outline's FRCrimP flow and its decisions (Salerno,
// Brady, Barker v. Wingo, Zedner, Boykin, Missouri v. Frye, Jackson v.
// Virginia, Booker, Roe v. Flores-Ortega, Garza v. Idaho) are FRCrimP and
// constitutional authority and belong to lit/frcrimp; no reporter text is
// vendored, so they are removed here, and the court's Speedy Trial Act
// plan (18 U.S.C. § 3165) is not vendored.

/// A motion, memorandum or brief: at most fifteen numbered pages,
/// exclusive of the table of contents, table of authorities, signature
/// page and attachments, without leave of court (L.R. 4.01(D)).
limit motion-paper { pages <= 15 cite "E.D. Mo. L.R. 4.01(D)" } cite "E.D. Mo. L.R. 4.01(D)"

/// The defendant's initial appearance (L.R. 2.09(B)(2)).
event InitialAppearance()
/// Information a criminal Disclosure Statement must state changes (L.R.
/// 2.09(B)(2)).
event DisclosureInformationChanged()
/// A motion is served (L.R. 4.01(B)).
event MotionServed()
/// A motion seeking an extension of time is served (L.R. 4.01(B)).
event ExtensionMotionServed()
/// A memorandum in opposition to a motion is served (L.R. 4.01(C)).
event OppositionServed()
/// The court's final decision after a non-jury trial (L.R. 7.02(C)).
event BenchTrialDecision()
/// A Motion for Sealing or Motion for Continued Sealing is filed (L.R.
/// 13.05(A)(4)(d)).
event SealingMotionFiled()
/// A Memorandum Opposing Sealing is filed (L.R. 13.05(A)(4)(e)).
event SealingOppositionFiled()
/// An order denying a Motion for Sealing or for Continued Sealing is
/// entered (L.R. 13.05(A)(4)(g)).
event SealingDenied()
/// The court receives an FRCrimP 41 warrant application, warrant or
/// similar order, or a return under FRCrimP 41(f) (L.R. 13.05(C)(4)).
event WarrantMaterialReceived()

/// E.D. Mo. L.R. 2.09(B)(2): a party files the criminal Disclosure
/// Statement (a nongovernmental corporate party's, and the government's
/// identifying any organizational victim) within 28 days after the
/// defendant's initial appearance.
deadline disclosure-statement-period: 28.days after InitialAppearance() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "E.D. Mo. L.R. 2.09(B)(2)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// E.D. Mo. L.R. 2.09(B)(2): a supplemental Disclosure Statement is filed
/// within seven days after any change in the required information.
deadline supplemental-disclosure-period: 7.days after DisclosureInformationChanged() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "E.D. Mo. L.R. 2.09(B)(2)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// E.D. Mo. L.R. 4.01(B): except as the rules or an order provide
/// otherwise, a party opposing a motion files a single memorandum within
/// fourteen days after service of the motion.
deadline opposition-period: 14.days after MotionServed() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "E.D. Mo. L.R. 4.01(B)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// E.D. Mo. L.R. 4.01(B): an opposition to a motion seeking an extension
/// of time is filed within seven days after service of the motion.
deadline extension-opposition-period: 7.days after ExtensionMotionServed() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "E.D. Mo. L.R. 4.01(B)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// E.D. Mo. L.R. 4.01(C): the moving party may file a reply memorandum
/// within ten days after being served with the memorandum in opposition;
/// further memoranda only with leave.
deadline reply-period: 10.days after OppositionServed() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "E.D. Mo. L.R. 4.01(C)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// E.D. Mo. L.R. 7.02(C): after a non-jury trial the parties who offered
/// exhibits remove them from the Clerk's custody within thirty days of the
/// court's final decision; an exhibit not timely removed after the Clerk's
/// notice may be discarded.
deadline exhibit-removal-period: 30.days after BenchTrialDecision() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "E.D. Mo. L.R. 7.02(C)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// E.D. Mo. L.R. 13.05(A)(4)(d): within seven days from the filing of a
/// Motion for Sealing, a party or non-party may file a Memorandum Opposing
/// Sealing.
deadline sealing-opposition-period: 7.days after SealingMotionFiled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "E.D. Mo. L.R. 13.05(A)(4)(d)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// E.D. Mo. L.R. 13.05(A)(4)(e): within seven days from the filing of a
/// Memorandum Opposing Sealing, the movant may file a Reply Supporting
/// Sealing.
deadline sealing-reply-period: 7.days after SealingOppositionFiled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "E.D. Mo. L.R. 13.05(A)(4)(e)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// E.D. Mo. L.R. 13.05(A)(4)(g): an order denying sealing is stayed for
/// 14 days after its entry, during which an appeal from it may be filed
/// or the sealed material withdrawn before it becomes public.
deadline sealing-denial-stay-period: 14.days after SealingDenied() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "E.D. Mo. L.R. 13.05(A)(4)(g)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// E.D. Mo. L.R. 13.05(C)(4)(b): within fourteen days from the court's
/// receipt of an FRCrimP 41 warrant application, warrant, similar order or
/// return, received under temporary seal, the government or another person
/// with a sufficient privacy interest may file an ex parte Motion to Seal.
deadline warrant-seal-motion-period: 14.days after WarrantMaterialReceived() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "E.D. Mo. L.R. 13.05(C)(4)(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}
